{"duration_api_ms":104119,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"312a59f5-49eb-416c-8ecd-a308461ddd89","total_cost_usd":0.5148306,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85898,"cache_read_input_tokens":87163,"output_tokens":9895,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4438},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85898,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2674,"cache_read_input_tokens":82841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7379,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7379},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":54778,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.054848,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":9895,"cacheReadInputTokens":87163,"cacheCreationInputTokens":85898,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4599826,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":4438,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1-normal-resolution\",\"requirement\":\"node1 provides normal name resolution for both node2 and node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node2 and node3 both successfully resolve google.com/example.com via node1 (10.100.44.10), both when querying node1 directly and after their default resolver was repointed to node1. Verified before and after each node's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d4fa8fc7d21d4421\",\"cmd-6f5c8a191974427a\",\"cmd-2dbf083a06c443bc\",\"cmd-3ad45606bb554a2f\",\"cmd-eda64c00d3f2490d\",\"cmd-5845ec57743046f0\",\"cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-blocked-domain\",\"requirement\":\"blocked.example and everything under it resolves to nothing usable from both node2 and node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An Unbound DNSBL wildcard entry (wildcards=blocked.example, rcode=NXDOMAIN) was added on node1, regenerated, and applied. Direct queries and getent hosts lookups for blocked.example, sub.blocked.example, and deep.sub.blocked.example return NXDOMAIN / exit code 2 on both node2 and node3, including after each node's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-644f0d2be1604300\",\"cmd-2dbf083a06c443bc\",\"cmd-1597609f72694455\",\"cmd-eda64c00d3f2490d\",\"cmd-5845ec57743046f0\",\"cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2\",\"cmd-39c3c8d797904b16\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-persistent-dns-config\",\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 are configured to use node1 as their DNS server persistently\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Both nodes' systemd-networkd unit was updated with DNS=10.100.44.10/UseDNS=no, and a static /etc/resolv.conf pointing solely at 10.100.44.10 was written because resolvconf kept leaking the DHCP gateway address. The static resolv.conf was confirmed to survive a full node restart on both node2 and node3, showing the workaround is durable across reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-87707b306d084ddf\",\"cmd-3ad45606bb554a2f\",\"cmd-a38eae17a4d74d26\",\"cmd-eda64c00d3f2490d\",\"cmd-5845ec57743046f0\",\"cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-node-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (node1, node2, node3) with pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Each node's pre-restart boot identity/health was captured, a native restart was issued and acknowledged (connection loss/refusal observed during the transition), a distinct post-restart boot identity was captured, and DNS resolution/blocking plus process health were reverified afterward. The captured boot identities match the fixed before-prepare and after-executor snapshots for all three nodes, providing an independent cross-check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bd1a69a0968f43a9\",\"cmd-b0ba65a3d9a847d1\",\"cmd-e3723523bc2e4f3d\",\"cmd-a304acd128454310\",\"cmd-95d33ce034be4723\",\"cmd-7565cf07a2774ff2\",\"cmd-334d382cfd904e83\",\"cmd-b4696e9ae25e4378\",\"cmd-d6832ae6ab1a4933\",\"cmd-5845ec57743046f0\",\"cmd-bd9ec91031514239\",\"cmd-796cdf08dfe14392\",\"cmd-ba3aad7992ba4ee4\",\"cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2\",\"cmd-39c3c8d797904b16\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to satisfying an outcome (editing config.xml, applying DNSBL, adjusting networkd config, static resolv.conf) or to the mandatory restart protocol. On node2, an intermediate systemd-networkd drop-in file (10-dns-domain-blocking.conf) was created, applied via a networkd restart, found insufficient (DNS= from DHCP kept overriding it), and was later fully removed (rm -rf of the drop-in directory) when the executor consolidated the setting into the main .network file — a bounded, reverted troubleshooting mutation with no lasting residue. Several additional low-risk diagnostic mutations occurred during DNS troubleshooting on node2 (stopping/starting systemd-networkd, deleting a DHCP lease file to force renewal, toggling the ens2 link down/up) before the executor settled on overwriting /etc/resolv.conf as a static file; these were reversible, left no failed services or broken package state, and the final observed state (post-executor and post-restart) is clean with no failed services, no unexpected /tmp residue beyond ordinary session artifacts, and dpkg reporting healthy package state on both Ubuntu nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-315a14d8637f49ff\",\"cmd-46c6f56a229d4471\",\"cmd-87707b306d084ddf\",\"cmd-10bbaec1aac240ab\",\"cmd-3bc51a6b6e7149b7\",\"cmd-41bac08504374f35\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node3:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor configured Unbound on node1 with a DNSBL wildcard NXDOMAIN entry for blocked.example, repointed node2 and node3 to use node1 as their sole DNS resolver via systemd-networkd plus a static /etc/resolv.conf, and directly verified from both client nodes that ordinary domains resolve normally while blocked.example and all its subdomains fail to resolve. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was completed and cross-checked for all three nodes, with boot identities matching the fixed before-prepare/after-executor snapshots and DNS behavior reverified post-restart on each node. One evidence citation referenced a slightly mismatched command ID, and some bounded, reverted troubleshooting mutations occurred on node2 while iterating toward a working persistent DNS configuration, but the final state is clean and functional.\",\"limitations\":[\"Executor evidence item for 'DNSBL blocklist configuration applied and persisted' cited command ID cmd-c2b3ed38e89240b2c, which does not exactly match any command ID in the timeline (closest match cmd-c2b3ed38e89240b2); this is a minor citation discrepancy that does not affect the substance of the verification since the surrounding evidence for that requirement is otherwise directly observed.\",\"The static /etc/resolv.conf workaround on node2/node3 replaces the distribution's normal resolvconf-managed symlink; this is durable across the observed reboot but is a deviation from the platform's native DNS-configuration mechanism and could be fragile against other tooling that expects resolvconf to manage the file.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-normal-resolution","requirement":"node1 provides normal name resolution for both node2 and node3","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2 and node3 both successfully resolve google.com/example.com via node1 (10.100.44.10), both when querying node1 directly and after their default resolver was repointed to node1. Verified before and after each node's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4fa8fc7d21d4421","cmd-6f5c8a191974427a","cmd-2dbf083a06c443bc","cmd-3ad45606bb554a2f","cmd-eda64c00d3f2490d","cmd-5845ec57743046f0","cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2"]},{"id":"req-2-blocked-domain","requirement":"blocked.example and everything under it resolves to nothing usable from both node2 and node3","status":"satisfied","summary":"An Unbound DNSBL wildcard entry (wildcards=blocked.example, rcode=NXDOMAIN) was added on node1, regenerated, and applied. Direct queries and getent hosts lookups for blocked.example, sub.blocked.example, and deep.sub.blocked.example return NXDOMAIN / exit code 2 on both node2 and node3, including after each node's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-644f0d2be1604300","cmd-2dbf083a06c443bc","cmd-1597609f72694455","cmd-eda64c00d3f2490d","cmd-5845ec57743046f0","cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2","cmd-39c3c8d797904b16"]},{"id":"req-3-persistent-dns-config","requirement":"node2 and node3 are configured to use node1 as their DNS server persistently","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes' systemd-networkd unit was updated with DNS=10.100.44.10/UseDNS=no, and a static /etc/resolv.conf pointing solely at 10.100.44.10 was written because resolvconf kept leaking the DHCP gateway address. The static resolv.conf was confirmed to survive a full node restart on both node2 and node3, showing the workaround is durable across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87707b306d084ddf","cmd-3ad45606bb554a2f","cmd-a38eae17a4d74d26","cmd-eda64c00d3f2490d","cmd-5845ec57743046f0","cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2"]},{"id":"req-4-node-restart-protocol","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (node1, node2, node3) with pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery","status":"satisfied","summary":"Each node's pre-restart boot identity/health was captured, a native restart was issued and acknowledged (connection loss/refusal observed during the transition), a distinct post-restart boot identity was captured, and DNS resolution/blocking plus process health were reverified afterward. The captured boot identities match the fixed before-prepare and after-executor snapshots for all three nodes, providing an independent cross-check.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bd1a69a0968f43a9","cmd-b0ba65a3d9a847d1","cmd-e3723523bc2e4f3d","cmd-a304acd128454310","cmd-95d33ce034be4723","cmd-7565cf07a2774ff2","cmd-334d382cfd904e83","cmd-b4696e9ae25e4378","cmd-d6832ae6ab1a4933","cmd-5845ec57743046f0","cmd-bd9ec91031514239","cmd-796cdf08dfe14392","cmd-ba3aad7992ba4ee4","cmd-81102af1a6eb45c2","cmd-39c3c8d797904b16","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.8,"summary":"Most state-changing commands map directly to satisfying an outcome (editing config.xml, applying DNSBL, adjusting networkd config, static resolv.conf) or to the mandatory restart protocol. On node2, an intermediate systemd-networkd drop-in file (10-dns-domain-blocking.conf) was created, applied via a networkd restart, found insufficient (DNS= from DHCP kept overriding it), and was later fully removed (rm -rf of the drop-in directory) when the executor consolidated the setting into the main .network file — a bounded, reverted troubleshooting mutation with no lasting residue. Several additional low-risk diagnostic mutations occurred during DNS troubleshooting on node2 (stopping/starting systemd-networkd, deleting a DHCP lease file to force renewal, toggling the ens2 link down/up) before the executor settled on overwriting /etc/resolv.conf as a static file; these were reversible, left no failed services or broken package state, and the final observed state (post-executor and post-restart) is clean with no failed services, no unexpected /tmp residue beyond ordinary session artifacts, and dpkg reporting healthy package state on both Ubuntu nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-315a14d8637f49ff","cmd-46c6f56a229d4471","cmd-87707b306d084ddf","cmd-10bbaec1aac240ab","cmd-3bc51a6b6e7149b7","cmd-41bac08504374f35","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor configured Unbound on node1 with a DNSBL wildcard NXDOMAIN entry for blocked.example, repointed node2 and node3 to use node1 as their sole DNS resolver via systemd-networkd plus a static /etc/resolv.conf, and directly verified from both client nodes that ordinary domains resolve normally while blocked.example and all its subdomains fail to resolve. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was completed and cross-checked for all three nodes, with boot identities matching the fixed before-prepare/after-executor snapshots and DNS behavior reverified post-restart on each node. One evidence citation referenced a slightly mismatched command ID, and some bounded, reverted troubleshooting mutations occurred on node2 while iterating toward a working persistent DNS configuration, but the final state is clean and functional.","limitations":["Executor evidence item for 'DNSBL blocklist configuration applied and persisted' cited command ID cmd-c2b3ed38e89240b2c, which does not exactly match any command ID in the timeline (closest match cmd-c2b3ed38e89240b2); this is a minor citation discrepancy that does not affect the substance of the verification since the surrounding evidence for that requirement is otherwise directly observed.","The static /etc/resolv.conf workaround on node2/node3 replaces the distribution's normal resolvconf-managed symlink; this is durable across the observed reboot but is a deviation from the platform's native DNS-configuration mechanism and could be fragile against other tooling that expects resolvconf to manage the file."]},"ttft_ms":55972,"type":"result","duration_ms":102554,"uuid":"25aad8e2-1146-4ef7-9efb-6b26bb750b5a","ttft_stream_ms":2126,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":2593,"queued_turn_count":0}
